# macOS native Steam bridge (Phase 24, D-07) -- the shim SOURCE
# (native/steam-bridge/generated/*.c/*.def) is generated but COMMITTED
# (deterministic, code-reviewable, pinned to the manifest sdkVersion). Only
# the built PE binary (compiled at packaging time, Plan 24-07) is ignored.
native/steam-bridge/generated/*.dll

# Phase 24 Plan 07 (R5): the pinned zig toolchain meta/downloadZig.ts
# extracts is a build-time-only tool, never bundled/committed.
/.build-tools/

# Phase 23.1 plan 05: lzma-native's real on-disk package root, resolved and
# baked in fresh by every build (meta/esbuildWorkerBundleShared.ts's
# writeLzmaNativeResolvedPaths()) -- machine-specific, regenerated every
# time, never committed. Mirrors spike 023's own resolved-paths.generated.cjs.
src/backend/storeManagers/steam/depot/lzmaNativeResolvedPaths.generated.cjs

# Knowledge graphs. graphify-out/ is the live standalone-`graphify`-CLI graph
# (large, regenerable via `graphify update .`, never committed).
# .planning/graphs/ is the retired GSD-skill duplicate -- ignored so it cannot
# come back.
graphify-out/
.planning/graphs/

# Local scratch working directory. Holds ad-hoc analysis files AND raw archived
# `gamelib-*.log` captures, which carry nile's plaintext PKCE material
# (`client_id`/`code_verifier`/`serial`) written by nile/user.ts:62. Ignored so
# that material can never be staged -- a prior session committed it once and
# had to amend it out.
scratchpad/

# Steam Spacewar (480) test AppID dropped next to the binary by the Steam
# bridge during local dev. Never part of a build.
steam_appid.txt

# Third-party Claude skill, installed from GitHub (`tt-a1i/archify`, MIT,
# v2.17.0-dev.1 on its "development" channel): 191 files / 7.3M, of which ~5M is
# `examples/` and `test/`. `skills-lock.json` at the repo root pins the install
# -- source, sourceType and a computedHash -- so the tree is reproducible from
# 4KB and does not need vendoring into a public fork.
#
# Vendoring it wholesale would also ship a subtly INCOMPLETE copy: the global
# `package-lock.json` rule at line 28 above silently excludes
# `archify/package-lock.json` (confirmed with `git check-ignore -v`), so the
# committed tree would NOT match the hash `skills-lock.json` records. If this is
# ever reversed and the skill is vendored deliberately, that rule needs a
# `!` negation for this path or the copy ships quietly wrong.
#
# The two skills that ARE tracked -- `sketch-findings-gamelib` and
# `spike-findings-gamelib` -- are first-party GameLib content, not external
# tooling, which is the line being drawn here.
.claude/skills/archify/

# Python bytecode. The `.planning/` tree carries stdlib-only planning gates
# (`*-gate.py`, discovered and run by meta/runPlanningGates.py). Two of their
# `__pycache__/*.pyc` files were tracked, which was always wrong and became
# actively wrong in two ways at once: renaming seam-parity-sweep.py orphaned
# its bytecode against a source file that no longer exists, and now that the
# gates run in CI every run regenerates these. Bytecode is a build product.
__pycache__/

# @opengsd/gsd-core runtime state (dispatch-isolation sentinel), rewritten on every
# workflow run. Machine-local, never source -- and untracked-but-unignored it fails
# the pre-push `prettier --check .`.
.gsd/
